WEBVTT

00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:04.030
No.

00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:06.400
Don't.

00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:10.170
No...

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:13.410
I said, no!

00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:41.640
Have you guys noticed the change?

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:43.270
Not especially...

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:46.040
It's been like that for a while, right?

00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:50.870
Not my hair.

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:52.570
I'm talking about Megumi.

00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:56.310
She's been lost in thought by herself lately.

00:00:56.380 --> 00:00:59.410
She's always out of it when I ask her something.

00:00:59.590 --> 00:01:01.710
I feel kinda distant from her.

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:06.930
Maybe because you said you weren't
joining us on our weekend trip.

00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:08.990
You're not going to Kurobe Shore?

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:11.630
Huh? Oh, no...

00:01:13.970 --> 00:01:16.840
I sure don't have any plans this weekend.

00:01:17.370 --> 00:01:19.670
Maybe that's why Megumi-san is...

00:01:19.910 --> 00:01:21.380
I'll go, I'll go.

00:01:21.610 --> 00:01:22.780
Great!

00:01:22.780 --> 00:01:25.610
You'll go too, right? Kanzato-kun's little brother?

00:01:25.610 --> 00:01:27.080
Oh, yes...

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:32.690
See? I definitely don't have anything going on.

00:01:32.990 --> 00:01:37.160
It's our reward for being the Half-Day Chiefs,

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:39.560
so I wanna include everyone and have fun.

00:01:40.030 --> 00:01:43.020
Actually, I won't have any plans for a long time...

00:01:43.730 --> 00:01:46.330
Wouldn't it be better to have
someone who can lead us?

00:01:47.570 --> 00:01:48.570
True...

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:50.270
More like a driver?

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:53.140
You have a favor to ask me or something?

00:01:53.140 --> 00:01:57.130
The coupon is for six people max,
so could you pay for yourself?

00:01:57.710 --> 00:02:01.550
But there are just six of us,
including Megumi-chan, right?

00:02:01.550 --> 00:02:03.710
Ayanagi City General Hospital

00:02:28.010 --> 00:02:29.440
Yumi-senpai!

00:02:46.030 --> 00:02:48.860
Kanjouni aragau nayo
Don't fight back your emotions

00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:51.200
sono ashiwo tomenna
Don't ever stop

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:55.360
taoreru nowa mada hayaize
It's too soon to fall down

00:02:56.140 --> 00:02:57.440
Breakin' through
Breakin' through

00:02:57.440 --> 00:02:59.140
uchinukeyo
Pierce through

00:02:59.140 --> 00:03:01.440
yamiwo hurihodoki
Free yourself from darkness

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:05.570
tadoritsuku bashowa hitotsusa
There is only one destination

00:03:06.550 --> 00:03:09.680
hurueru sora
Quaking sky

00:03:11.590 --> 00:03:15.150
kazewa naniwo tsugeru
What is the wind telling me?

00:03:16.690 --> 00:03:21.260
Tadashii datoka soujanai toka
Right or wrong

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:24.200
kudaranai ronsouwa
Nonsensical arguments

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:26.830
kieya shinai kedo
Never go away

00:03:26.830 --> 00:03:31.410
shinjita kotowo shinjinuku koto
Believe what you believe in

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:33.210
sono sakini bokurawa
At the end of it all

00:03:33.210 --> 00:03:36.840
hikari mitsukeru darou
We will find the light

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:41.800
saa tokihanate ima
Now is the time to release it

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:45.150
kanjouni aragau nayo
Don't fight back your emotions

00:03:45.150 --> 00:03:47.390
sono ashiwo tomenna
Don't ever stop

00:03:47.390 --> 00:03:51.290
taoreru nowa mada hayaize
It's too soon to fall down

00:03:52.330 --> 00:03:53.630
Breakin' through
Breakin' through

00:03:53.630 --> 00:03:55.330
uchinukeyo
Pierce through

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:57.570
yamiwo hurihodoki
Free yourself from darkness

00:03:57.570 --> 00:04:01.590
tadoritsuku bashowa hitotsusa
There is only one destination

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:18.690
Jun is already waiting outside.

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:19.650
Oh, I see...

00:04:24.290 --> 00:04:25.660
Have a safe trip.

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:29.690
Okay... I'm leaving now.

00:04:39.940 --> 00:04:41.880
Sorry to intrude...

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:44.080
Don't worry about it, Tasaka-senpai.

00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:46.710
Now it's three guys and three girls.

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:48.980
Shin, isn't this like?

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:50.580
What?

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:52.450
You know?

00:04:52.450 --> 00:04:53.720
A group date trip?

00:04:53.720 --> 00:04:55.020
Yeah, that's it!

00:04:55.790 --> 00:04:56.820
Idiot...

00:04:56.820 --> 00:04:58.790
But there are seven of us including me...

00:04:58.890 --> 00:05:04.560
I'm glad you seem a lot better than
when we last saw you at the hospital.

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:06.030
Thanks...

00:05:06.130 --> 00:05:09.500
Your brother is the Chief at Ayanagi Station, right?

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:10.710
Yes...

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:14.940
The Chief saved me when I had my accident.

00:05:15.810 --> 00:05:18.040
Could you give him my gratitude?

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:20.180
Sure... I'll let him know.

00:05:20.180 --> 00:05:20.320
Okazaki Takashi
Tasaka Yumi
Sure... I'll let him know.

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:21.840
Okazaki Takashi
Tasaka Yumi

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:26.490
You're?

00:05:26.490 --> 00:05:29.720
I was at the hospital too...

00:05:30.090 --> 00:05:31.060
No.

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:33.800
Didn't I do Shadow Extraction
on you the other day at school?

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:35.400
Is that true, Kanaru?

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:37.400
Well... um... yes.

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:40.700
Senpai, didn't I ask you to stop doing that?

00:05:40.700 --> 00:05:41.840
I'm sorry...

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:44.240
She was begging me.

00:05:44.970 --> 00:05:46.810
B-but it was quite a while ago.

00:05:46.810 --> 00:05:49.470
No matter when it was, Shadow Extraction is bad!

00:05:49.940 --> 00:05:51.040
I'm sorry!

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:06.660
Oh, um, what were we talking about?

00:06:06.660 --> 00:06:09.990
Tasaka-senpai and I did Shadow Extraction...

00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:11.160
That's right!

00:06:11.430 --> 00:06:13.970
Kanaru, no more Shadow Extraction!

00:06:13.970 --> 00:06:15.090
I'm sorry!

00:06:15.540 --> 00:06:17.370
Hey, your conversation is going nowhere!

00:06:25.350 --> 00:06:26.070
Come in.

00:06:30.920 --> 00:06:34.380
Eiko, I told you to stay away from here.

00:06:34.490 --> 00:06:36.550
I wasn't told that I was prohibited completely.

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:40.120
I need your approval, Chief.

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:45.260
This isn't your normal job.

00:06:46.170 --> 00:06:47.690
Excuse us!

00:06:48.700 --> 00:06:49.640
Hello?

00:06:49.640 --> 00:06:50.070
Sema Koji/Yuko
Hello?

00:06:50.070 --> 00:06:53.010
Sema Koji/Yuko
My, welcome everyone.

00:06:53.370 --> 00:06:55.580
Come right in.

00:06:55.580 --> 00:06:57.110
Thank you for accommodating us!

00:06:57.110 --> 00:06:58.550
How energetic.

00:06:58.550 --> 00:07:00.520
Your room is to your left at the end.

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:01.580
Hello.

00:07:01.580 --> 00:07:03.420
Well, it's been a while.

00:07:03.420 --> 00:07:04.990
We're here again.

00:07:04.990 --> 00:07:06.690
You remember us?

00:07:06.690 --> 00:07:07.880
Of course!

00:07:09.020 --> 00:07:10.490
Are you girls still dancing?

00:07:10.490 --> 00:07:11.330
Yes.

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:13.690
Are you still running this place by yourself?

00:07:13.690 --> 00:07:14.560
Yes...

00:07:14.560 --> 00:07:17.130
My husband hasn't gotten back yet.

00:07:17.130 --> 00:07:19.220
Look how tough I've become.

00:07:20.130 --> 00:07:22.160
Kayano, you've been here before?

00:07:22.640 --> 00:07:25.440
Yeah, we came here to train
together two years ago.

00:07:25.710 --> 00:07:27.940
To put a bratty newcomer in her place.

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:31.070
What? It was because I was a
newcomer with potential, right?

00:07:32.980 --> 00:07:33.850
Thank you for accommodating us.

00:07:33.850 --> 00:07:35.380
Sure. Make yourselves at home.

00:07:35.380 --> 00:07:35.620
The puppy's room is in the back.

00:07:35.620 --> 00:07:36.650
The puppy's room is in the back.
Shin-niichan.

00:07:36.650 --> 00:07:37.390
The puppy's room is in the back.

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:38.080
Okay.

00:07:38.650 --> 00:07:41.120
Did Megumi-san have a little brother?

00:07:41.660 --> 00:07:42.690
A brother?

00:07:42.690 --> 00:07:44.210
I haven't heard of him.

00:07:45.330 --> 00:07:46.120
I see...

00:07:51.800 --> 00:07:56.930
Permission: Access to data regarding accidents
near Toyama Bay over the past ten years.

00:08:03.210 --> 00:08:06.150
Sema Koji

00:08:06.150 --> 00:08:10.020
Vanished at sea while sailing
along the coast of Toyama Bay.

00:08:16.960 --> 00:08:20.900
Can't you be more, like... enthusiastic?

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:22.990
Maybe, uh, fool around by the water?

00:08:23.100 --> 00:08:24.830
I don't think so.

00:08:31.270 --> 00:08:32.000
Jun!

00:08:33.410 --> 00:08:36.930
The vending machine was a
lot farther than you described.

00:08:37.210 --> 00:08:40.280
Isn't that better than to think it's
really far away from the beginning?

00:08:40.280 --> 00:08:41.350
Hmm... I guess.

00:08:41.350 --> 00:08:43.320
It wasn't that bad.

00:08:44.950 --> 00:08:46.750
Wasn't Takuro-kun with you, too?

00:08:46.750 --> 00:08:48.220
Huh? I don't think so.

00:08:49.360 --> 00:08:50.460
What about senpai?

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:51.430
Thanks...

00:08:51.430 --> 00:08:53.390
Tasaka-senpai is over there.

00:09:10.980 --> 00:09:12.040
Senpai!

00:09:13.680 --> 00:09:14.380
Kayano?

00:09:16.750 --> 00:09:17.740
What's the matter?

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:18.920
Well...

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:20.610
...Did you think I was gonna commit suicide?

00:09:22.690 --> 00:09:23.710
I see...

00:09:24.490 --> 00:09:26.620
Is that why you invited me here?

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:29.620
I'll be fine.

00:09:34.640 --> 00:09:35.530
I'm okay.

00:09:35.870 --> 00:09:36.860
Thanks, Kayano.

00:09:41.080 --> 00:09:43.070
I'm not thinking about dying anymore.

00:09:45.950 --> 00:09:48.540
I was just confirming that here.

00:09:48.680 --> 00:09:49.780
Senpai.

00:09:52.690 --> 00:09:53.620
I'm just joking...

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:06.890
We watched the sunset here last time, too.

00:10:07.340 --> 00:10:09.360
We were so exhausted.

00:10:09.940 --> 00:10:12.060
We were training since that morning.

00:10:12.770 --> 00:10:15.500
You were like a monster.

00:10:15.940 --> 00:10:18.340
You were such a bitter dancer.

00:10:18.950 --> 00:10:21.520
You would give up so easily, even if you
knew you could do some of the moves.

00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:22.850
Really?

00:10:22.850 --> 00:10:23.840
Really.

00:10:24.920 --> 00:10:27.150
Are you getting that way again?

00:10:27.150 --> 00:10:27.780
What?

00:10:28.160 --> 00:10:30.390
Are you trying to ignore something?

00:10:33.130 --> 00:10:34.530
I apologize if I'm mistaken.

00:10:35.360 --> 00:10:35.990
It's just...

00:10:40.640 --> 00:10:42.130
I want you to...

00:10:42.470 --> 00:10:44.100
What if it's something I can't do?

00:10:45.240 --> 00:10:46.430
I tried hard...

00:10:47.940 --> 00:10:51.840
Can I give up, if it's something that
I tried so hard but couldn't do?

00:10:57.180 --> 00:10:58.980
N-nevermind.

00:10:59.150 --> 00:10:59.950
I'm sorry.

00:11:00.720 --> 00:11:01.620
Kayano...

00:11:01.620 --> 00:11:04.490
Remember? We made a promise that time.

00:11:04.490 --> 00:11:08.790
I won't ignore things. I won't
give up on the things I can do...

00:11:09.200 --> 00:11:10.030
I'm sorry!

00:11:12.970 --> 00:11:14.740
We should get going soon.

00:11:14.740 --> 00:11:15.460
Yeah.

00:11:46.930 --> 00:11:47.990
Those girls...

00:11:48.570 --> 00:11:52.600
They came to stay here for a few days
at the end of summer two years ago.

00:11:56.140 --> 00:12:00.810
It seemed that Megumi-chan, with
braids, had some kind of problem.

00:12:01.650 --> 00:12:05.020
She seemed a lot better by
the time they left, though.

00:12:05.720 --> 00:12:06.780
I see...

00:12:08.290 --> 00:12:11.160
Um... Is that your husband?

00:12:11.930 --> 00:12:15.830
Mm-hmm. He disappeared while
he was out at sea ten years ago.

00:12:16.560 --> 00:12:18.230
The only thing he left was our boat.

00:12:19.500 --> 00:12:20.690
Ten years ago...

00:12:30.710 --> 00:12:33.710
I'm not too good with hot baths,
so I'm going to get out now.

00:12:33.710 --> 00:12:34.200
Okay...

00:12:36.420 --> 00:12:39.180
I feel bad that Yumi-san can't
come in because of her injury.

00:12:39.550 --> 00:12:41.020
Oh... You're right.

00:12:48.630 --> 00:12:50.790
You're amazing.

00:12:51.700 --> 00:12:53.720
You're, like, perfect.

00:12:55.140 --> 00:12:56.260
D-do you think so?

00:12:57.240 --> 00:12:58.970
Ahh, hey guys!

00:13:03.980 --> 00:13:04.440
Huh?

00:13:05.750 --> 00:13:07.870
There, there. It's gonna be tasty.

00:13:10.420 --> 00:13:14.320
I didn't know it was the girls' turn to take a bath.

00:13:14.660 --> 00:13:17.120
Plus, I couldn't see anything through all the steam.

00:13:17.760 --> 00:13:18.730
Eight.

00:13:18.960 --> 00:13:20.450
Let him go, Kayano.

00:13:20.690 --> 00:13:22.060
He seems to be telling the truth.

00:13:22.630 --> 00:13:23.290
Nine.

00:13:23.960 --> 00:13:27.370
Just so you know, I'm still growing!

00:13:28.100 --> 00:13:29.090
Then!?

00:13:29.840 --> 00:13:32.010
You'll never see me, not even
when I'm all done growing!

00:13:32.010 --> 00:13:32.670
Ten!

00:13:33.340 --> 00:13:35.940
Besides, where have you been all day?

00:13:35.940 --> 00:13:37.910
Well... you know.

00:13:38.280 --> 00:13:39.140
Exploring.

00:13:40.610 --> 00:13:42.510
Umm... Eleven.

00:13:42.620 --> 00:13:44.210
Inui-san, that's B.S.

00:13:44.420 --> 00:13:45.720
Not again!

00:13:48.560 --> 00:13:49.820
What do you think?

00:13:50.560 --> 00:13:57.160
They're missing cases at different areas
and times, but there are similarities.

00:13:57.600 --> 00:14:01.860
Every case record reports witnesses
seeing "a feather in the air."

00:14:05.640 --> 00:14:09.080
What do you think this feather's significance is?

00:14:17.590 --> 00:14:20.520
Same time, same place...

00:14:21.290 --> 00:14:24.880
What was so different between those
who vanished and those who remained?

00:15:30.960 --> 00:15:31.930
Dammit!

00:15:33.230 --> 00:15:35.090
I knew it.

00:15:43.470 --> 00:15:44.460
Takuro!

00:15:45.370 --> 00:15:46.840
What are you doing?

00:15:47.170 --> 00:15:49.800
What am I-? Umm...

00:15:50.410 --> 00:15:53.240
Practicing to fight using your
Persona, or something like that?

00:15:53.550 --> 00:15:56.140
Practicing... more like training.

00:15:56.320 --> 00:15:59.550
You know, I put you guys through
so much trouble last time.

00:15:59.750 --> 00:16:01.120
Impressive.

00:16:01.120 --> 00:16:02.320
Shut up...

00:16:03.020 --> 00:16:03.860
No.

00:16:03.860 --> 00:16:04.520
Huh?

00:16:05.590 --> 00:16:07.560
Don't do that...

00:16:09.660 --> 00:16:12.500
Why would you do that!? What's the point!?

00:16:12.900 --> 00:16:14.530
What do you mean by that!?

00:16:14.670 --> 00:16:18.340
Who knows when that flat-haired
guy will show up again!?

00:16:18.340 --> 00:16:20.340
Then, we can get the police to...

00:16:20.340 --> 00:16:22.310
We'd be dead before the police arrived!

00:16:22.480 --> 00:16:25.930
We'd die anyway because of your useless Persona!

00:16:26.280 --> 00:16:27.180
Kayano...

00:16:27.310 --> 00:16:28.550
That's why I'm...

00:16:28.550 --> 00:16:30.050
I'm begging you, stop!

00:16:30.050 --> 00:16:31.620
Do you wanna die, Takuro!?

00:16:31.620 --> 00:16:33.640
Why would I-!?

00:16:34.050 --> 00:16:35.720
Even if you use a Persona...

00:16:35.720 --> 00:16:36.490
Kayano!

00:16:36.490 --> 00:16:37.520
Nobody will...

00:16:37.520 --> 00:16:38.290
Kayano!

00:16:44.400 --> 00:16:47.130
I have to tell you two something.

00:16:48.270 --> 00:16:49.170
What is it?

00:16:49.970 --> 00:16:53.500
Tasaka-senpai... There's a
possibility she also has a Persona.

00:16:56.110 --> 00:16:57.870
Just like Takuro's friend...

00:16:57.950 --> 00:17:00.510
She might have gotten attacked
because of her Persona.

00:17:01.320 --> 00:17:02.250
Her Persona?

00:17:03.720 --> 00:17:06.190
There are people who are trying
to collect the Personas of others.

00:17:06.590 --> 00:17:07.990
I've been attacked several times.

00:17:08.320 --> 00:17:10.520
The flat-haired guy is one of them.

00:17:11.060 --> 00:17:15.090
I don't know what exactly is
going on, but I'm sure of that.

00:17:15.960 --> 00:17:16.860
And...

00:17:17.200 --> 00:17:18.890
We can't count on the police.

00:17:19.030 --> 00:17:19.970
Why not?

00:17:19.970 --> 00:17:21.000
Now that you mention it...

00:17:21.000 --> 00:17:24.000
The detectives wanted to keep
the karaoke incident a secret,

00:17:24.000 --> 00:17:26.670
and the article in the newspaper was so...

00:17:30.110 --> 00:17:31.480
Is your brother?

00:17:31.480 --> 00:17:33.310
I'll talk to you guys about that some other time.

00:17:35.380 --> 00:17:37.870
Please let Takuro keep training, Kayano.

00:17:40.790 --> 00:17:44.920
We may have to fight them again.

00:17:45.960 --> 00:17:48.330
Then, I'll also have to... with Takuro...

00:17:51.370 --> 00:17:52.350
Otherwise...

00:17:54.940 --> 00:17:55.800
But...

00:18:18.060 --> 00:18:20.790
But what if you end up hurting someone that way?

00:18:20.790 --> 00:18:21.560
What if someone die...

00:18:21.560 --> 00:18:23.000
We can't let that get to us...

00:18:23.000 --> 00:18:24.030
We should!

00:18:24.030 --> 00:18:25.500
If only I were...

00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:29.160
If I were... able to use "it" right...

00:18:29.500 --> 00:18:31.490
Kayano... Are you also?

00:18:33.110 --> 00:18:34.630
There you guys are.

00:18:34.940 --> 00:18:37.740
I got worried with all five of you disappearing.

00:18:38.250 --> 00:18:41.040
If it were just a boy and girl
missing, I'd let that slide...

00:18:41.420 --> 00:18:42.420
Five of us?

00:18:42.420 --> 00:18:44.410
You guys aren't with Yumi-san?

00:18:53.360 --> 00:18:54.090
Kayano!
Megumi!

00:18:54.730 --> 00:18:55.560
Megumi-san!

00:19:10.440 --> 00:19:11.070
Senpai!

00:19:12.750 --> 00:19:14.810
Dammit! I'll-!

00:19:19.590 --> 00:19:20.110
GO!

00:19:20.850 --> 00:19:21.620
All right!

00:19:54.050 --> 00:19:55.390
Yumi-senpai!

00:19:59.430 --> 00:20:01.050
Senpai!

00:21:03.790 --> 00:21:05.120
It's hurt...

00:21:12.770 --> 00:21:15.500
Her heart is broken...

00:21:16.540 --> 00:21:17.200
It's already...

00:21:46.670 --> 00:21:53.570
omotai kusariwo
The heavy chain

00:21:53.570 --> 00:21:59.350
ima hazushite agemashou
I will take it off for you

00:21:59.350 --> 00:22:04.450
jiyuuni naretara
Once you're free

00:22:04.450 --> 00:22:11.660
kokowo habataite yukeruwa
You'll be able to fly away

00:22:11.660 --> 00:22:18.230
atashiga samatage
I stood in your way

00:22:18.230 --> 00:22:26.410
ubatte kita madaminu sekai e
and took that world you haven't seen

00:22:26.410 --> 00:22:31.180
tamerau nonara
If you're going to hesitate

00:22:31.180 --> 00:22:39.950
huriharatte ageru sono udewo
I will free that arm for you

00:22:40.190 --> 00:22:44.490
soshite tookue
Then to faraway

00:22:44.490 --> 00:22:50.700
dekirudake tookue
As far away as possible

00:22:50.700 --> 00:22:54.030
aishiteruno
"I love you"

00:22:54.030 --> 00:22:57.700
ikanaideyo
"Don't leave me"

00:22:57.700 --> 00:23:04.200
koware chaukara
I will break

00:23:14.490 --> 00:23:16.180
A wandering wish.

00:23:17.360 --> 00:23:19.790
No way to rise to the surface.

00:23:20.060 --> 00:23:22.590
No way to return to the mental sea's depths.

00:23:24.030 --> 00:23:25.930
Covering pain with pain.

00:23:26.630 --> 00:23:30.360
The wound, concealed by burdened chaos.

00:23:31.740 --> 00:23:33.670
There's no past that I want to return to.

00:23:34.670 --> 00:23:36.970
There were no guardians to give me love.

00:23:37.840 --> 00:23:39.070
Even so,

00:23:39.750 --> 00:23:41.870
there exists a person I miss.
